#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/names.phtml:40
msgid ""
"Each arc on the circumference is one of the top surnames in the tree, ranked "
"by how many marriages that surname appears in (as husband or wife). Ribbons "
"between two arcs encode the number of marriages between those surnames. The "
"ribbon thickness is proportional to that count. The diagram is symmetric, so "
"a Schmidt × Müller marriage contributes equally to both arcs. Self-loops on "
"an arc represent endogamous marriages where husband and wife share a surname."
msgstr ""
"Chaque arc sur la circonférence représente l'un des noms de famille les plus "
"fréquents dans l'arbre, classé selon le nombre de mariages où le nom "
"apparaît (comme mari ou épouse). Les rubans entre deux arcs codent le nombre "
"de mariages entre ces noms de famille. L'épaisseur du ruban est "
"proportionnelle à ce nombre. Le diagramme est symétrique. Un mariage Schmidt "
"× Müller contribue donc autant aux deux arcs. Les boucles sur un arc "
"représentent les mariages endogames où le mari et l'épouse partagent le même "
"nom de famille."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/overview.phtml:210
msgid ""
"Each band links a parent's occupation to the occupation of one of their "
"children. The band's thickness encodes the count: thicker bands mean more "
"children recorded in that trade after a parent. Only children whose father "
"or mother also has a recorded occupation are counted. Hover any band to see "
"the exact parent trade → child trade, the number of children, and a few of "
"them by name."
msgstr ""
"Chaque bande relie la profession d'un parent à celle de l'un de ses enfants. "
"L'épaisseur de la bande indique le nombre d'enfants : plus la bande est "
"épaisse, plus il y a d'enfants recensés dans ce métier après leur parent. "
"Seuls les enfants dont le père ou la mère a également une profession "
"enregistrée sont pris en compte. Passez la souris sur n'importe quelle bande "
"pour voir la correspondance exacte entre la profession du parent et celle de "
"l'enfant, le nombre d'enfants concernés et les noms de certains d'entre eux."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/names.phtml:36
msgid ""
"Each band stands for one of the most common given names in the tree. The "
"band's vertical thickness in a given decade shows how many individuals born "
"in that decade carried that name. The silhouette layout centers each band "
"around zero, so the chart reads as relative magnitudes. Hover any band to "
"see absolute counts and its peak decade."
msgstr ""
"Chaque bande représente l'un des prénoms les plus courants dans l'arbre. "
"L'épaisseur verticale de la bande pour une décennie donnée indique combien "
"de personnes nées au cours de cette décennie portaient ce prénom. La "
"disposition en silhouette centre chaque bande autour de zéro. Le graphique "
"se lit donc comme des magnitudes relatives. Survolez une bande pour afficher "
"les chiffres absolus et sa décennie de pointe."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/life-span.phtml:652
msgid ""
"Each cell counts the births recorded in one period (a row) and one calendar "
"month (a column), with the count printed inside it. The period is 25 years "
"wide and widens in steps when the tree spans so many centuries that narrower "
"rows would be too many to read. The more births fell in that period and "
"month, the more saturated the cell; a near-blank cell means few or none. "
"Reading down a column shows whether a month stayed busy across the periods, "
"reading along a row shows how one period spread its births over the year. "
"Only dates with both a known year and month are placed. Leading and trailing "
"periods without a single recorded birth are dropped, while an empty period "
"between two recorded ones stays as a blank band so a gap in the records is "
"not hidden."
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/life-span.phtml:672
msgid ""
"Each cell counts the deaths recorded in one period (a row) and one calendar "
"month (a column), with the count printed inside it. The period is 25 years "
"wide and widens in steps when the tree spans so many centuries that narrower "
"rows would be too many to read. The more deaths fell in that period and "
"month, the more saturated the cell; a near-blank cell means few or none. "
"Reading down a column shows whether a month stayed busy across the periods, "
"reading along a row shows how one period spread its deaths over the year. "
"Only dates with both a known year and month are placed. Leading and trailing "
"periods without a single recorded death are dropped, while an empty period "
"between two recorded ones stays as a blank band so a gap in the records is "
"not hidden."
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/life-span.phtml:619
msgid ""
"Each dot marks a year in which several families each lost two or more "
"children"
msgstr ""
"Chaque point correspond à une année au cours de laquelle plusieurs familles "
"ont perdu chacune au moins deux enfants"

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/places.phtml:54
msgid ""
"Each flow shows individuals who were born in one country and died in "
"another. The flow's thickness encodes the count: thicker bands mean more "
"migrations along that path. Same-country trajectories are excluded — they're "
"not migration. Hover any band to see the exact source → destination and "
"individual count. Only individuals with both a recorded birth place and a "
"recorded death place appear, so emigrants who lost contact and have no "
"recorded death place are missing: read the diagram as a lower bound on real "
"migration."
msgstr ""
"Chaque flux représente les personnes nées dans un pays et décédées dans un "
"autre. L'épaisseur du flux correspond au nombre de cas : plus la bande est "
"épaisse, plus il y a eu de migrations sur cet itinéraire. Les trajectoires "
"au sein d’un même pays sont exclues — elles ne constituent pas des "
"migrations. Passez la souris sur n’importe quelle bande pour voir la source "
"→ la destination exacte et le nombre de personnes concernées. Seules les "
"personnes pour lesquelles le lieu de naissance et le lieu de décès sont tous "
"deux enregistrés apparaissent ; les émigrants qui ont perdu tout contact et "
"dont le lieu de décès n’est pas enregistré ne sont donc pas pris en compte : "
"considérez ce diagramme comme une estimation minimale des migrations réelles."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/places.phtml:66
msgid ""
"Each individual is bucketed by the great-circle distance in kilometers "
"between their birth place and death place. Only individuals whose birth AND "
"death place both carry map coordinates are counted. The coordinates are read "
"from the event itself (a PLAC:MAP sub-tag) or from the place list of "
"webtrees, and the module reads no external geocoder. The chart therefore "
"covers the documentation-limited subset of records that were geocoded at "
"all, a lower bound on real mobility rather than a complete picture. The "
"chart is hidden when too few individuals qualify."
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/family.phtml:381
msgid ""
"Each point is the average number of children per family for that century, "
"computed from every family whose earliest marriage falls in it. Hover a "
"point to see how many families the average is based on. A century is only "
"drawn once at least five dated families back it; below that a single large "
"or childless family would swing the mean by tenths of a child and render a "
"spiky, unrepresentative point."
msgstr ""
"Chaque point correspond au nombre moyen d'enfants par famille pour le siècle "
"concerné, calculé à partir de toutes les familles dont le premier mariage a "
"eu lieu au cours de ce siècle. Passez la souris sur un point pour voir sur "
"combien de familles repose cette moyenne. Un siècle n'est représenté qu'une "
"seule fois s'il est étayé par au moins cinq familles datées ; en dessous de "
"ce seuil, une seule famille nombreuse ou sans enfant ferait varier la "
"moyenne de quelques dixièmes d'enfant et donnerait lieu à un point "
"irrégulier et non représentatif."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/family.phtml:297
msgid ""
"Each point shows the average parental age in full years. The two lines are "
"computed separately for fathers and mothers, as shown by the legend. A "
"decade is only drawn for a given parent if at least five parents of that sex "
"appear in it. Decades with fewer samples are dropped from that line, so a "
"single outlier cannot distort the trend. Hover any point to see how many "
"parents the average is based on."
msgstr ""
"Chaque point indique l'âge moyen des parents en années entières. Les deux "
"lignes sont calculées séparément pour les pères et les mères, comme "
"l'indique la légende. Une décennie n'est tracée pour un parent donné que si "
"au moins cinq parents de ce sexe y figurent. Les décennies comptant moins "
"d'échantillons sont retirées de cette ligne, afin qu'un seul cas atypique ne "
"fausse pas la tendance. Survolez un point pour voir sur combien de parents "
"la moyenne repose."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/tree-health.phtml:528
msgid "Each step is one parent–child link upward."
msgstr "Chaque étape correspond à un lien parent–enfant vers le haut."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/tree-health.phtml:627
msgid "Each step is one partnership further along the line."
msgstr "Chaque étape correspond à un lien parent–enfant vers le haut."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/tree-health.phtml:200
msgid ""
"Each tile is one connected sub-tree: a group of individuals tied together by "
"parentage or marriage, with no link to any other sub-tree. The tile area is "
"proportional to the number of members, the largest first. The label is the "
"most common surname within that sub-tree — so the same surname can mark "
"several separate sub-trees when a family line is not yet connected to the "
"rest of the tree. The final tile sums up every sub-tree beyond the ten "
"largest."
msgstr ""
"Chaque tuile représente un sous-arbre connecté : un groupe d’individus liés "
"par filiation ou par alliance, sans aucun lien avec un autre sous-arbre. La "
"superficie de la tuile est proportionnelle au nombre de membres, les plus "
"grands apparaissant en premier. L'étiquette correspond au nom de famille le "
"plus courant au sein de ce sous-arbre — ainsi, un même nom de famille peut "
"désigner plusieurs sous-arbres distincts lorsqu'une lignée familiale n'est "
"pas encore reliée au reste de l'arbre. La dernière tuile regroupe tous les "
"sous-arbres au-delà des dix plus grands."

#: resources/views/modules/statistics-chart/tabs/life-span.phtml:607
msgid ""
"Each year's recorded death count is compared with the surrounding eleven-"
"year window. A year is flagged when its count lies at least two standard "
"deviations above the window's mean, and the flagged years that stand out "
"most are listed in chronological order. The marker behind each bar shows the "
"window median as the expected baseline; mean and median sit close together "
"but are not identical. Only years with a full window on both sides are "
"considered, so the most recent and oldest years are never flagged. Read a "
"flagged year as one that stands out against the recorded baseline, not "
"automatically as real excess mortality: denser record-keeping, an import "
"batch, or round-year date clustering can lift a single year's count much as "
"a true epidemic, war or famine would. Where the death places of a year fall "
"in a covered region and period, the year is annotated with the historical "
"event it coincides with: a temporal note, never a stated cause of death; "
"coverage is limited to broadly-documented events and can be extended via the "
"project repository."
msgstr ""

